<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 45 0 R
/T (Vue 3's Composition API is arguably more approachable for new developers, and Nuxt's directory conventions are intuitive. However, the gap narrows substantially with TypeScript: both frameworks have excellent TS support, and React's explicit mental model \(props down, events up\) aligns well with Atomic Design's unidirectional data flow. )
/E (Vue 3's Composition API is arguably more approachable for new developers, and Nuxt's directory conventions are intuitive. However, the gap narrows substantially with TypeScript: both frameworks have excellent TS support, and React's explicit mental model \(props down, events up\) aligns well with Atomic Design's unidirectional data flow. )
